{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Come on back. I-95 was a parking lot this morning. A mattress fell off a truck and everybody just sat there.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): And this heat, ninety-something and sticky. My kid's soccer got canceled 'cause the field is soup from the storm. Neighbor's grandkid plays goalie and will not shut up about it. You follow any of that rec league stuff?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (NURSE): Ha. Fair enough. Let me get your numbers.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (NURSE): Blood pressure is one oh nine over seventy-seven. Temp is thirty-eight point three. Weight today fifty-two kilograms.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (NURSE): Last time in March you were sixty-eight. Your last pressure was one-forty. Pulse ninety-two, uh, sorry, I double-counted, pulse is eighty-eight.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): Hi, I'm Dr. Shah. Your partner over there looks pretty anxious, knee bouncing. What brought you in today?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Can't sleep.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): Even when the baby is sleeping?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (DOCTOR): You look tearful. Crying a lot at home too?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (DOCTOR): When did the not sleeping and the crying start?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm. Since the hospital. Or after. Dunno. Maybe before.",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (DOCTOR): You're six weeks out from the delivery. The sleep and the tears you can't place. Hospital, or after, maybe even before.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (DOCTOR): I need to ask straight. Any thoughts of hurting yourself?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any thoughts of hurting the baby?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (DOCTOR): Temp came back thirty-eight point three. Chills? Feel hot?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): Cramps low in your belly?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Some.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): Heavy bleeding, soaking a pad?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any cough, trouble breathing, chest pain?",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (DOCTOR): Still on the prenatal vitamin, once a day, by mouth?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (DOCTOR): The ibuprofen from after the delivery, that's finished, you're off it?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (DOCTOR): Allergies to any medicine or food?",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (DOCTOR): So, six weeks postpartum, you can't sleep even when the baby sleeps, you're tearful, some low cramps, a fever on the thermometer, no chills, no heavy bleeding, no thoughts of harming yourself or the baby. Vitamin daily, ibuprofen stopped. My working impression is postpartum depression, provisional. With that temperature I can't rule out an infection or a thyroid piece.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (DOCTOR): Thursday morning the nurse takes bloods, a TSH and a blood count. Come fasting, water only after midnight. If those are borderline we do the third test, a free T4. If the cramping does not settle, a pelvic scan.",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'll see you in two weeks. Have your partner take one night feed so you can lie down, and call us or 988 if those harm thoughts show up.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay."
 ],
